| `agents/doc_reviewer/` | Reviews the documentation against the doc style: deterministic findings first, then one judged edit per chunk, each gated on `make check-docs`. | `make doc-review`; `make doc-review-apply` | [`models.default`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`corpus.served_visibilities`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Applying spends model calls; a red gate triggers journalled restoration, with `RollbackError` naming failed restores and retaining the journal for startup replay. A finding on a file the corpus does not place at a served level, or whose file states a level outside them on disk now or none that can be read, is withheld: it is reported with the reason and never reaches a prompt. When the corpus or config cannot be read, every finding is withheld. | [doc-style.md](../guides/doc-style.md) | always |
